"""Import a headerless AI-label CSV into every matching command row.

Example: ./scripts/import_labels --db cmds.duckdb --table SHELL_INPUTS \
    --labels labels/shell_inputs_luna_labels.csv

Columns: label,shell_input or label,pgm,arg1,arg2,... . A process with no arguments
has two columns; an empty argument is a separate empty column. Labels must be
malicious, benign, or unknown. Matching uses exact text and full argument arrays
across all datasets. Conflicting known AI labels produce warnings with the old
label, new label, and command, and are overwritten. Repeated CSV commands apply
in file order. All updates commit in one transaction; malformed input rolls
everything back. The final label is
recomputed using human override, then known AI label, then dataset label.
CSV records are held in memory; database matching and updates use bulk joins.
"""

from _import_labels import main

if __name__ == '__main__':
    main(__doc__)
